<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Hungary</h1><p class="st-meta">895 CE – 1000 CE (approx.) · capital Esztergom</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Hungarian state of the Árpád dynasty in the Carpathian basin, from the conquest of 895 to Stephen's coronation as king in 1000.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pecheneg</a> attacks drove them from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etelkoz">Etelköz</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hungarian-tribal-federation">Hungarian tribal federation</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> in 895. By the first years of the 10th century they held the whole basin, and in 907 they destroyed a Bavarian army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a>, securing the conquest.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>For half a century Hungarian horsemen raided <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, until Otto I defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lechfeld">Lechfeld</a> in 955. The grand princes then centralised power: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksony">Taksony</a> and especially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geza-grand-prince-of-the-hungarians">Géza</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Esztergom</a>, curbed tribal chiefs and invited Western missionaries. Géza was baptised and married his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-i-of-hungary">Vajk</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gisela-of-bavaria">Gisela of Bavaria</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geza-grand-prince-of-the-hungarians">Géza</a>'s son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-i-of-hungary">Vajk</a>, baptised Stephen, defeated the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/koppany">Koppány</a> and was crowned king on Christmas Day 1000 (or 1 January 1001) with a crown from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-sylvester-ii">Pope Sylvester II</a>, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-hungary-1000-1301">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1000-1301).</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-hungary.jpg" alt="Principality of Hungary" width="320" height="161"><figcaption>Image: Oppashi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hungary_(895-1000).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>895 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Esztergom</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Árpád, Taksony, Géza</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism; Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Grand Principality of Hungary, Hungarian Principality</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=948&amp;focus=principality-of-hungary" aria-label="Principality of Hungary on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5117 504 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Hungary lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5437 760L5446 783M5437 760L5557 785M5437 760L5417 706"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5446 783h0M5557 785h0M5417 706h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5437 760h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5437 760h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Esztergom. <a href="/atlas?year=948&amp;focus=principality-of-hungary">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
